From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:46:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 176/207] server: deadline_s reaches the engine over HTTP; a
 deadline outranks a late token's finish

T5's OBJECT to dadaa0e24: the OpenAI request plan copies only listed fields into the request, and deadline_s was not
listed, so over HTTP the field never reached chat.zig (a valid one did nothing, bad ones were not refused). It is now
forwarded for chat and legacy completions.

A token the engine gives after the server's deadline cancel may be EOS, hit a stop string or reach max_tokens; its
reason used to win and hide the deadline. Now a reply the server ended at its deadline is always finish "deadline",
with every late token kept in text, usage and ids. A deadline that passes after the reply already ended (a stop
string's own cancel) is not counted.

request_deadline_http_test (test-request-deadline-host): through openai.run, chat and completions, whole and
streamed: deadline_s ends the reply with finish deadline, the late token, usage, ids and receipt; no field and a
deadline never met give the same reply and stream choices; 0, -1, "300", true and 1e7 are a 400 before the engine;
a late EOS, stop string or token cap after the deadline still ends "deadline" with 4 tokens.
